# MCO Wizard - Visual SNLP Generator
# Features for the MCO Wizard implementation

@optional Workflow Library
>Create a comprehensive workflow library system that allows users to browse, search, and select from various MCO workflow templates. The library should include:
>
>1. Categorized sections for different use cases (coding assistants, research agents, creative workflows, etc.)
>2. Visual previews of each workflow with clear descriptions of their purpose
>3. Popularity and community ratings for each workflow
>4. Tags and filtering options to help users find relevant workflows
>5. Clear distinction between official pre-built workflows and community contributions
>6. Import functionality for adding custom workflows to the library
>
>The library should serve as an educational resource that helps users understand different MCO orchestration patterns through practical examples.

@optional Visual SNLP Editor
>Develop an intuitive visual editor for SNLP files that abstracts away syntax complexity while preserving the full power of MCO. The editor should include:
>
>1. Side-by-side view of all four SNLP files (core, sc, features, styles) with synchronized navigation
>2. Toggle between "Values Only" mode (for beginners) and "Full Edit" mode (for advanced users)
>3. Syntax highlighting and auto-completion for SNLP markers and structures
>4. Drag-and-drop functionality for reordering sections within files
>5. Context-aware editing assistance that suggests appropriate content based on the current section
>6. Visual indicators showing relationships between elements across different files
>7. Collapsible sections for managing complex workflows
>
>The editor should make SNLP creation feel as natural as filling out a well-designed form while maintaining the structural integrity required by MCO.

@optional Real-time Validation Engine
>Implement a sophisticated validation engine that provides immediate, helpful feedback during the SNLP creation process. The validation engine should:
>
>1. Use the same validation logic as the official MCO CLI tool
>2. Highlight errors and warnings with clear visual indicators
>3. Provide specific, actionable suggestions for fixing validation issues
>4. Check for both syntax correctness and semantic coherence
>5. Validate relationships between elements across different files
>6. Show an overall "health score" for the workflow
>7. Prevent download of invalid workflows while explaining exactly what needs to be fixed
>
>The validation should feel like a helpful assistant rather than a gatekeeper, guiding users toward creating effective workflows.

@optional Progressive Revelation Visualizer
>Create a unique visualization tool that helps users understand and design for MCO's progressive revelation approach. This feature should:
>
>1. Show a timeline view of how information will be revealed to the agent during execution
>2. Allow users to simulate the agent experience at different points in the workflow
>3. Highlight which elements from each file are active at each stage
>4. Provide guidance on optimal information distribution across files
>5. Warn about potential information sequencing issues
>6. Include examples of effective progressive revelation patterns
>
>This visualizer should make the abstract concept of progressive revelation concrete and actionable for users.

@optional Guided Workflow Creation
>Develop a step-by-step guided creation process for users building workflows from scratch. This feature should:
>
>1. Offer multiple starting points based on the user's goal and experience level
>2. Break down the workflow creation process into logical, manageable steps
>3. Provide contextual examples and suggestions at each step
>4. Allow users to skip ahead or go back as needed
>5. Save progress automatically to prevent work loss
>6. Include templates for common sections (agent definitions, success criteria patterns, etc.)
>7. Gradually introduce more advanced concepts as users progress
>
>The guided creation should feel like working with an expert who's helping you translate your ideas into effective MCO workflows.

@optional Export and Integration Options
>Implement flexible export options that support various integration scenarios. This feature should:
>
>1. Allow downloading individual SNLP files or complete workflow packages
>2. Provide direct integration with common development environments
>3. Generate code snippets for integrating the workflow with different agent frameworks
>4. Include documentation specific to the created workflow
>5. Support version control with change history and comparison tools
>6. Enable sharing workflows directly to the community repository
>7. Provide options for private or public workflow publishing
>
>The export options should make it seamless to move from creation to implementation in real projects.

@optional Interactive Tutorial System
>Create an embedded tutorial system that helps new users learn MCO concepts while building actual workflows. This feature should:
>
>1. Offer interactive walkthroughs of key MCO concepts and best practices
>2. Provide contextual help that appears when users encounter new concepts
>3. Include a library of short video demonstrations for complex features
>4. Offer progressive challenges that build skills incrementally
>5. Celebrate user achievements with meaningful feedback
>6. Allow users to experiment safely in a sandbox environment
>7. Include before/after examples showing how MCO improves agent performance
>
>The tutorial system should transform learning MCO from a technical challenge into an engaging discovery process.

